<title>AUSTRALIA: TNT year net profit slides.</title>
<headline>TNT year net profit slides.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    92.30 vs 119.08</p>
<p>    Net					9.84 vs 40.01</p>
<p>    Abnormal			 loss 65.38 vs loss 9.47</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)		nil vs nil</p>
<p>NOTE: TNT ltd is an international transport and logistics group. Operating and net profits are on an equity accounted basis.  </p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)		nil vs nil</p>
<p>    Sales (billion)			7.33 vs 6.49</p>
<p>    Other income			  75.07 vs 72.20</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			    1.20 vs 5.1</p>
<p>    Tax				     67.50 vs 58.28</p>
<p>    Interest				84.21 vs 86.34</p>
<p>    Depreciation			 112.28 vs 105.14</p>
<p>    Minorities		    credit 1.02 vs charge 1.45</p>
<p>NOTE: TNT paid preference dividends of A$25.23 million compared to A$21.67 million the previous year.  </p>
<p>NOTE: Operating profit/loss before abnormals and tax by industry segment.</p>
<p>    Time-sensitive		     101.87 vs 92.31</p>
<p>    Logistics			     85.27 vs 47.86</p>
<p>    Non time-sensitive	   loss 35.95 vs profit 18.83</p>
<p>    Aircraft management		 13.83 vs 5.86</p>
<p>    Unallocated/corporate	loss 26.11 vs loss 22.81</p>
<p>    Other				    1.46 vs 1.32</p>
<p>NOTE: Operating profit/loss before abnormals and tax by geographic segment.</p>
<p>    Australia and Asia	   loss 21.71 vs profit 18.13</p>
<p>    Europe				 171.76 vs 112.90</p>
<p>    Americas			  loss 9.90 vs profit 12.33</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
